From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: admit the exact Uke NFC L7E resource

Uke OEM DT 94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57 describes the
POCO tag supply as L7E in qcom/uke-sm8635.dtsi and the exact ldoe7
resource in qcom/cliffs-regulators.dtsi. Native release 33 leaves the
tag deferred because this resource is outside the reviewed allowlist.

Retain OEM constraints and the existing provider's command-DB validation,
request ownership and failure paths. This adds no guessed voltage or
board value and does not establish physical RF acceptance. The tag
transport retains its separate exact POCO model admission.

--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
@@ -2012,7 +2012,8 @@
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob5") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob12") &&
 	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob8") &&
-	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldod3"))
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldod3") &&
+	    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoe7"))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	aggr_vreg->addr = cmd_db_read_addr(aggr_vreg->resource_name);
